//@version=6
// ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//    QQQ 5-MIN ORB — REPLICATION ATTEMPT (Zarattini & Aziz 2023)
//    v1.1.4-rep · 2026-07-22 · FROZEN for the Premium campaign
//
//    v1.1.4 (audit round 4 — diagnostics and contamination guards only;
//    the entry/stop/target/EOD path is unchanged from v1.1.3):
//     · Fill-bar-closed trades now contribute to the leverage/risk/
//       gap-through audits (previously bypassed — and those are the
//       trades most likely to contain a gap-through-stop).
//     · Fill-bar target classified by exit PRICE vs the estimated
//       target level (within 1.5 ticks), not by profit sign.
//     · Mean leverage excess displayed when breaches exist.
//     · SYMBOL GUARD: refuses to run on anything but QQQ.
//     · Entry comments carry a parameter fingerprint (risk/R/cap), so
//       an altered-input run cannot masquerade as the frozen config.
//
//    v1.1.3 (audit round 3, still pre-result):
//     · LEVERAGE STATEMENT CORRECTED. Position size is capped using the
//       first-bar-close estimate; emulator margin enforcement is
//       disabled; actual fills MAY slightly exceed 4x. Frequency and
//       magnitude are audited (strict counter, max, mean excess) and
//       reconstructable offline from qty x entry / running equity.
//       Exact at-fill enforcement is impossible when size is fixed at
//       submission — the paper sized at the recorded 9:35 price and so
//       never faced this. Frozen as a documented approximation.
//     · Breach counter now strict (> 4x exactly, was > 4.004x, which
//       would have missed every real trim-scale overage). Adds max
//       leverage and mean excess.
//     · Ambiguity check moved BEFORE target correction, so the fill
//       bar is tested against the ESTIMATED target that was genuinely
//       live during it, not the corrected one (false-positive fix).
//
//    v1.1.2: margin_long/short 25 -> 0. With margin enforcement on, a
//    position sized to exactly the 4x cap from the ESTIMATED entry
//    (D3) opens fractionally over 4x at the actual fill, and the
//    emulator margin-calls a 1-share trim — creating phantom same-bar
//    micro-trades (two "trades" per session) that would corrupt the
//    H2 trade-count reconciliation. The paper models no margin calls;
//    it simply caps size at 4x. Faithful implementation: emulator
//    margin checks OFF, the 4x rule enforced solely by the explicit
//    qtyLev sizing cap (D7). Observed live before any valid deep run.
//
//    v1.1.1 fixes a cross-session state bug found by the invariant halt
//    on first live compile (v1.1.0 never produced a valid run): an EOD
//    immediate close is detected one execution late, on the NEXT
//    session's first bar, where the stale cleanup zeroed a freshly
//    armed signal — the following fill then correctly tripped
//    "fill without an armed signal". Fixes: EOD block now clears its
//    own state synchronously; the late-close cleanup can no longer
//    clobber a same-execution signal; fill-bar-target and ambiguity
//    tests use trade entry/exit times instead of the corrected flag.
// ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//    Implements Zarattini & Aziz (2023), SSRN 4416622, for QQQ:
//     · First 5-min bar rises -> BUY at the start of the second bar;
//       falls -> SELL SHORT; open == close -> no trade (see D2).
//     · Stop at the first bar's LOW (long) / HIGH (short).
//     · Target at 10x the entry-to-stop distance.
//     · Neither hit -> liquidate at the market close.
//     · Size so a stop costs 1% of current equity; 4x leverage cap;
//       $25,000 start; $0.0005/share commission; no slippage.
//
//    v1.1.0 supersedes v1.0.0, which was NEVER RUN. v1.0.0 defects
//    (external audit, pre-execution): (a) compile blocker — global
//    mutated inside a function; (b) CRITICAL — bracket submitted one
//    bar after the fill, leaving the entire second bar unprotected;
//    (c) ambiguity counter could never fire and could mis-attribute
//    pre-bracket movement; (d) fill-vs-intent audits absent;
//    (e) intrabar fill model not frozen.
//
//    ─── BRACKET TIMING (the v1.1.0 fix) ──────────────────────────────
//    strategy.exit is submitted in the SAME execution as strategy.entry
//    (first bar's close). An exit bound by from_entry activates when the
//    entry fills, so the STOP — the first bar's extreme, exactly known
//    in advance — protects from the second bar's first tick. The TARGET
//    needs the actual entry price, unknowable until the fill; it is
//    placed initially from the estimated entry (first bar's close) and
//    re-issued from strategy.position_avg_price at the next execution.
//    Residual approximation: during the fill bar only, the target sits
//    at 11x(estimated-entry error) from its true level, on a level 10R
//    away — a touch there in one 5-min bar is near-impossible, and
//    fill-bar target exits are counted (nFillBarTargets) so the
//    magnitude of this approximation is measurable, not assumed.
//    calc_on_order_fills stays FALSE: deterministic once-per-bar
//    execution, and TradingView warns that recalculation-on-fill can
//    create unrealistic historical behavior.
//
//    ─── INTRABAR FILL MODEL — FROZEN ─────────────────────────────────
//    use_bar_magnifier = false, set explicitly in the declaration so
//    Strategy Properties cannot decide it invisibly. Rationale: the
//    magnifier's lower-timeframe coverage is finite, so a 2016-2023 run
//    would mix fill models across eras. One uniform (coarser) model
//    beats a silently inconsistent one. A magnifier-ON sensitivity run
//    may be added as a separately labelled exploratory item.
//
//    ─── WHAT SURVIVES INTO A DEEP EXPORT ─────────────────────────────
//    Deep Backtesting renders nothing on the chart; the table below
//    reflects CHART-LOADED history only. Provenance that DOES survive
//    into the exported List of Trades:
//     · Entry comment  "QQQREP|<L|S>|v<SCRIPT_VERSION>"
//     · Exit comments  "TGT" / "STP" / "EOD" (comment_profit /
//       comment_loss / EOD close) — every exit self-classifies.
//    Counters that do NOT survive deep export: dojis, zero-qty skips,
//    ambiguous bars, session count. Mitigation: verify these on the
//    chart-loaded window (where the table works) as a spot check, and
//    audit the deep export offline — actual leverage is reconstructable
//    from qty x entry / running equity, and gap-through-stop events
//    appear as same-bar stop exits with losses exceeding ~1% of equity.
//
//    ─── DOCUMENTED DEVIATIONS FROM THE PAPER ─────────────────────────
//     D1 · Paper trades at recorded 9:35:00 prices; emulator fills at
//          the second bar's open. Feed and rounding differences apply.
//     D2 · "About the same" (no-trade condition) unquantified in the
//          paper; implemented as open == close exactly; dojis counted.
//     D3 · Sizing estimates entry at the first bar's close (true entry
//          unknowable at submission). Fill-vs-intent audits below
//          measure the consequence instead of assuming it away.
//     D4 · EOD flat via strategy.close_all(immediately = true) on
//          session.islastbar_regular — fills at that bar's close.
//          Calendar-triggered, never price-triggered: the ONLY
//          permitted use of `immediately` in this project. Handles
//          half-days correctly by construction.
//     D5 · Emulator assumes an intrabar path when stop and target both
//          lie inside one bar; such bars are counted (nAmbiguous) over
//          the chart-loaded window.
//     D7 · Position size is capped using the first-bar close estimate.
//          Emulator margin enforcement is disabled. Actual fills may
//          slightly exceed 4x; frequency and magnitude are audited
//          on-chart (strict count, max, mean excess) and offline from
//          the export. This is NOT at-fill 4x enforcement.
//     D6 · Deep data coverage decides the tested period. If 5m data
//          does not reach 2016, this is a PARTIAL replication and the
//          ledger must say so.
// ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
strategy("QQQ 5m ORB — Replication (Z&A 2023)", "QQQ REP",
     overlay                 = true,
     initial_capital         = 25000,
     default_qty_type        = strategy.fixed,
     default_qty_value       = 0,
     commission_type         = strategy.commission.cash_per_contract,
     commission_value        = 0.0005,
     slippage                = 0,
     pyramiding              = 0,
     margin_long             = 0,
     margin_short            = 0,
     calc_on_every_tick      = false,
     calc_on_order_fills     = false,
     process_orders_on_close = false,
     use_bar_magnifier       = false,
     max_labels_count        = 50)

SCRIPT_VERSION = "1.1.4-rep"

gP = "Paper parameters (change = no longer the replication)"
riskPct = input.float(1.0, "Risk per trade (% of equity)", minval = 0.1, step = 0.1, group = gP)
rMult = input.float(10.0, "Profit target (R multiple)", minval = 1, step = 0.5, group = gP)
levCap = input.float(4.0, "Leverage cap (x equity)", minval = 1, step = 0.5, group = gP)
showTable = input.bool(true, "Show diagnostics (chart-loaded only)", group = gP)

// ─── Guards ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
fiveMin = timeframe.isintraday and timeframe.in_seconds() == 300
symOk = syminfo.ticker == "QQQ"
chartOk = fiveMin and chart.is_standard and symOk
rthFirst = session.isfirstbar_regular
rthLast = session.islastbar_regular

// ─── Invariants (array pattern: functions cannot assign globals) ────
var array<int> invN = array.new<int>(1, 0)
inv(_c, _m) =>
    if _c
        array.set(invN, 0, array.get(invN, 0) + 1)
        runtime.error("INVARIANT FAILURE · " + _m + " · " + str.tostring(time))

// ─── Counters (chart-loaded population only — see header) ───────────
var int nSessions = 0
var int nDoji = 0
var int nSignals = 0
var int nZeroQty = 0
var int nEodExits = 0
var int nAmbiguous = 0
var int nFillBarTargets = 0     // target exit on the fill bar (est-target era)
var int nGapThroughStop = 0     // entry filled at/beyond the stop level
var int nLevBreach = 0          // actual exposure exceeded the cap (strict)
var float maxLev = 0.0
var float sumLevExcess = 0.0
var int nRiskBreach = 0         // actual risk exceeded intent by >20%

// ─── Per-signal state ───────────────────────────────────────────────
var int armedDir = 0
var float armedStop = na
var float eqAtSignal = na
var bool corrected = false
var float activeStop = na
var float activeTarg = na
var int seenClosed = 0
bool armedThisBar = false

if rthFirst
    inv(strategy.position_size != 0, "position survived into a new session")
    strategy.cancel_all()
    nSessions += 1
    armedDir := 0
    corrected := false
    activeStop := na
    activeTarg := na

// ─── Signal + FULL bracket at the first bar's close ─────────────────
// Guard `not rthLast`: on a one-bar session the entry would otherwise
// fill at the NEXT session's open.
if chartOk and barstate.isconfirmed and rthFirst and not rthLast
    dir = close > open ? 1 : close < open ? -1 : 0
    if dir == 0
        nDoji += 1
    else
        stopPx = dir == 1 ? low : high
        riskPerShare = math.abs(close - stopPx)
        if riskPerShare > 0
            qtyRisk = math.floor(strategy.equity * riskPct / 100 / riskPerShare)
            qtyLev = math.floor(strategy.equity * levCap / close)
            qty = math.min(qtyRisk, qtyLev)
            if qty < 1
                nZeroQty += 1
            else
                armedDir := dir
                armedStop := stopPx
                eqAtSignal := strategy.equity
                corrected := false
                estTarg = close + dir * rMult * riskPerShare      // D3 estimate
                activeStop := stopPx
                activeTarg := estTarg
                nSignals += 1
                armedThisBar := true
                strategy.entry("REP", dir == 1 ? strategy.long : strategy.short,
                     qty = qty, comment = "QQQREP|" + (dir == 1 ? "L" : "S") + "|v" + SCRIPT_VERSION + "|P" + str.tostring(riskPct, "#.#") + "/" + str.tostring(rMult, "#.#") + "/" + str.tostring(levCap, "#.#"))
                // Same-execution bracket: activates on the entry fill,
                // so the (exact) stop covers the fill bar's first tick.
                strategy.exit("X", from_entry = "REP", stop = stopPx, limit = estTarg,
                     comment_profit = "TGT", comment_loss = "STP")

// ─── Ambiguity + fill-bar-target counters ───────────────────────────
// Runs BEFORE the correction block deliberately: on the fill bar,
// activeTarg still holds the ESTIMATED target — the level genuinely
// live during that bar. The correction updates it only for later bars.
// Evaluated on every bar where the bracket was live at any point: the
// position is open now, OR a trade closed during this bar. This is the
// v1.0.0 fix — the old check ran only while still open, so any bar
// that actually filled a bracket leg was skipped by construction.
tradeClosedThisBar = strategy.closedtrades > seenClosed
closedIdx = strategy.closedtrades - 1
// "Closed on THIS bar" — by exit time, not by inference from flags.
closedOnThisBar = tradeClosedThisBar and strategy.closedtrades.exit_time(closedIdx) >= time
bracketLive = not na(activeStop) and not armedThisBar and (strategy.position_size != 0 or closedOnThisBar)
if bracketLive
    d = armedDir
    hitStop = d == 1 ? low <= activeStop : high >= activeStop
    hitTarg = d == 1 ? high >= activeTarg : low <= activeTarg
    if hitStop and hitTarg
        nAmbiguous += 1
if tradeClosedThisBar
    closedOnFillBar = strategy.closedtrades.entry_time(closedIdx) >= time
    if closedOnFillBar
        // Classify by exit PRICE against the estimated target level —
        // profit sign is unreliable when the entry gapped through a level.
        xp = strategy.closedtrades.exit_price(closedIdx)
        if not na(activeTarg) and math.abs(xp - activeTarg) <= syminfo.mintick * 1.5
            nFillBarTargets += 1
        // Fill-bar-closed trades bypass the open-position audit block,
        // so run the same audits here from the closed-trade record.
        if not corrected and armedDir != 0 and not na(armedStop) and not na(eqAtSignal)
            cep = strategy.closedtrades.entry_price(closedIdx)
            cqty = math.abs(strategy.closedtrades.size(closedIdx))
            cLev = cqty * cep / eqAtSignal
            maxLev := math.max(maxLev, cLev)
            if cLev > levCap
                nLevBreach += 1
                sumLevExcess += cLev - levCap
            if cqty * math.abs(cep - armedStop) / eqAtSignal * 100 > riskPct * 1.2
                nRiskBreach += 1
            if armedDir == 1 ? cep <= armedStop : cep >= armedStop
                nGapThroughStop += 1
            corrected := true
    seenClosed := strategy.closedtrades
    // Late-detected close (e.g. yesterday's EOD): clear ONLY stale
    // state. Never clobber a signal armed in this same execution —
    // that was the v1.1.0 crash.
    if not armedThisBar
        activeStop := na
        activeTarg := na
        armedDir := 0

// ─── One bar after the fill: true-entry target + fill audits ────────
if strategy.position_size != 0 and not corrected
    ep = strategy.position_avg_price
    d = strategy.position_size > 0 ? 1 : -1
    inv(armedDir == 0, "fill without an armed signal")
    inv(d != armedDir, "direction changed between signal and fill")
    trueTarg = ep + d * rMult * math.abs(ep - armedStop)
    strategy.exit("X", from_entry = "REP", stop = armedStop, limit = trueTarg,
         comment_profit = "TGT", comment_loss = "STP")
    activeTarg := trueTarg
    // D3 audits: measure the sizing deviation instead of assuming it.
    qtyNow = math.abs(strategy.position_size)
    actualRiskPct = qtyNow * math.abs(ep - armedStop) / eqAtSignal * 100
    actualLev = qtyNow * ep / eqAtSignal
    maxLev := math.max(maxLev, actualLev)
    if actualLev > levCap
        nLevBreach += 1
        sumLevExcess += actualLev - levCap
    if actualRiskPct > riskPct * 1.2
        nRiskBreach += 1
    if d == 1 ? ep <= armedStop : ep >= armedStop
        nGapThroughStop += 1
    corrected := true

// ─── EOD flat (D4 — sole permitted `immediately`) ───────────────────
if rthLast and strategy.position_size != 0
    nEodExits += 1
    strategy.close_all(comment = "EOD", immediately = true)
    // The immediate fill lands on THIS tick but bookkeeping above has
    // already run. Clear state here so the next session starts clean
    // whether or not closedtrades has incremented yet.
    activeStop := na
    activeTarg := na
    armedDir := 0
    corrected := false
    seenClosed := math.max(seenClosed, strategy.closedtrades)

// ─── Diagnostics (CHART-LOADED ONLY) ────────────────────────────────
var table t = table.new(position.top_right, 2, 13, bgcolor = color.new(color.black, 0), border_width = 1, border_color = color.new(color.gray, 80))
r(_i, _k, _v, _c) =>
    table.cell(t, 0, _i, _k, text_color = color.new(color.white, 45), text_size = size.tiny, text_halign = text.align_left)
    table.cell(t, 1, _i, _v, text_color = _c, text_size = size.tiny, text_halign = text.align_right)

if showTable and barstate.islast
    table.clear(t, 0, 0, 1, 12)
    if not chartOk
        r(0, "REJECTED", not symOk ? "USE QQQ — wrong symbol" : not chart.is_standard ? "NON-STANDARD DATA" : "USE 5m CHART", color.orange)
    else
        iv = array.get(invN, 0)
        r(0, "⚠", "CHART-LOADED ONLY — NOT DEEP REPORT", color.orange)
        r(1, "MODEL", "QQQ-REP v" + SCRIPT_VERSION + " | " + syminfo.tickerid, color.white)
        r(2, "INVARIANTS", iv == 0 ? "clean" : str.tostring(iv), iv == 0 ? #22c55e : #ef4444)
        r(3, "Sessions", str.tostring(nSessions), color.white)
        r(4, "Signals / dojis / zero-qty", str.tostring(nSignals) + " / " + str.tostring(nDoji) + " / " + str.tostring(nZeroQty), color.white)
        r(5, "EOD liquidations", str.tostring(nEodExits), color.new(color.white, 40))
        r(6, "Ambiguous bars", str.tostring(nAmbiguous), nAmbiguous > 0 ? color.orange : color.new(color.white, 40))
        r(7, "Fill-bar targets (est-targ era)", str.tostring(nFillBarTargets), nFillBarTargets > 0 ? color.orange : color.new(color.white, 40))
        r(8, "Gap-through-stop entries", str.tostring(nGapThroughStop), nGapThroughStop > 0 ? color.orange : color.new(color.white, 40))
        meanExc = nLevBreach > 0 ? str.tostring(sumLevExcess / nLevBreach, "#.####") : "—"
        r(9, "Lev>cap n/max/mean-exc/risk", str.tostring(nLevBreach) + " / " + str.tostring(maxLev, "#.###") + "x / " + meanExc + " / " + str.tostring(nRiskBreach), (nLevBreach + nRiskBreach) > 0 ? color.orange : color.new(color.white, 40))
        r(10, "Closed trades", str.tostring(strategy.closedtrades), color.white)
        r(11, "Net profit", str.tostring(strategy.netprofit, "#.##"), strategy.netprofit > 0 ? #22c55e : #ef4444)
        r(12, "Equity", str.tostring(strategy.equity, "#"), color.new(color.white, 40))
